      "writtenOn": "2022-06-30T15:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a simple signal with 4 states.  Does it make sense to (Switch) ?\n\nThis has 2 benefits.\n1) Inverts the logic so that `true` cases are entered, which is a little easier for the reader to understand quicker.\n2) Enumerates the actual conditions the logic is execute so one knows the exact 2 conditions at a glance why we are entering (WAITING_FOR_RESUME, RESUMED)\n\ne.g.\nfor (auto client : registered_clients_) {\n  switch (client.second) {\n    case ClientState::PAUSED:\n    case ClientState::WAITING_FOR_PAUSE:\n      break;\n    case WAITING_FOR_RESUME:\n    case RESUMED:\n        client.second \u003d ClientState::WAITING_FOR_PAUSE;\n        client.first-\u003eOnPause();\n  }\n}",
      "revId": "7332df884aff7b20d36892db5f0bd3438436b6f8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
